// Expected: f1 at one session and at two.
//
// A guard says the attacker did not alter a message in transit. It does not
// say the sender held an honest value to begin with. Alice's fresh value goes
// to Bob unguarded, and Bob and Carol then forward it over two guarded legs to
// Dave, who hashes it. Replacing it on the one unguarded leg therefore decides
// what Dave uses, two relays later, without any guard being defeated.
//
// This needs both halves of forward execution: the substitution lands on Bob,
// whose own block uses nothing, and its consequence has to be carried to Carol
// and then to Dave before the query can see it.

attacker[active]

principal Alice[
	generates ftr_x
]

principal Bob[]
principal Carol[]

Alice -> Bob: ftr_x
Bob -> Carol: [ftr_x]
Carol -> Dave: [ftr_x]

principal Dave[
	ftr_y = HASH(ftr_x)
]

queries[
	freshness? ftr_x
]
